because I was getting tummy aches.

516
00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.590
It was too much sugar.

517
00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:00.090
Yeah.

518
00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:03.010
So he said, what won't you eat?

519
00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:06.890
And I said, I won't eat Mike and Ike's, and I won't eat Red Hots.

520
00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:08.570
So he put Red Hots in there.

521
00:22:10.310 --> 00:22:16.610
So if you ever see Mike and Ike's or Red Hots in my candy dispenser, it was per my request,

522
00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:19.430
because I was needing to stop my candy eating.

523
00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:24.470
Well, I noticed that your fingernail polish is the exact same color as your coffee mug.

524
00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:27.250
It's kind of a pinky purple in this episode.

525
00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:32.410
I don't know why I was allowed to do that, but it matches my dress for the fundraiser very well.

526
00:22:32.510 --> 00:22:32.790
Mm-hmm.

527
00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:37.690
Aaron and Angela, Pam, Kevin, and Jim are all now going to go to the parking lot.

528
00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:38.870
They're going to check in on Andy.

529
00:22:39.110 --> 00:22:39.670
Like, what's he doing?

530
00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:40.570
He's sitting in his car.

531
00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:41.130
What's happening?

532
00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:41.570
Mm-hmm.

533
00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:43.050
Aaron is filming him.

534
00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:46.510
She said, hey, can we just film you saying that you're fine and everything's normal?

535
00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:48.790
Because they're worried he might hurt Robert.

536
00:22:49.690 --> 00:22:51.790
He says, guys, I am fine.

537
00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:54.430
I'm just picking up Aaron for the fundraiser tonight.

538
00:22:55.070 --> 00:22:57.670
Kevin is the one that's like, that's going to be weird.

539
00:22:58.430 --> 00:22:58.610
Mm-hmm.

540
00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:00.570
Like, Kevin's the one that clocks in on this?

541
00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:00.870
Yeah.

542
00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:01.430
I was like, what?

543
00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:04.650
Kevin is the voice of reason through this entire episode.

544
00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:05.190
I know.

545
00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:06.470
It's a wonderful turn.

546
00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:09.970
Well, Brian could not get through this scene.

547
00:23:10.270 --> 00:23:11.570
He kept getting tickled.

548
00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:15.430
It's in the bloopers that I watched all 19 minutes of, and I want you to hear it.

549
00:23:15.890 --> 00:23:16.830
I'm picking up Aaron.

550
00:23:16.970 --> 00:23:17.830
We're going to the fundraiser.

551
00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:19.350
Oh, great.

552
00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:20.030
That sounds good.

553
00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:20.550
Wait, what?

554
00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:22.390
You're going to the fundraiser tonight?

555
00:23:23.070 --> 00:23:24.110
That's going to be weird.

556
00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:25.250
Why would that be weird?

557
00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.570
Yeah, Kevin, come on.

558
00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:27.310
It's going to be fine.

559
00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:28.370
It's not weird at all.

560
00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:34.290
Um, am I the only, am I, uh, um, ready?

561
00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:35.030
Mm-hmm.

562
00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:36.310
Yeah, that's not weird at all.

563
00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:37.330
Oh, boy.

564
00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:41.670
Oh, my gosh.

565
00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:42.710
It's John.

566
00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:44.450
It's John and Brian.

567
00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:46.150
Yeah, John is messing with him.

568
00:23:46.590 --> 00:23:50.150
Brian was trying so hard, if you watch it, to say the line.

569
00:23:50.910 --> 00:23:55.790
So he's trying to kind of laugh through it, like, um, uh, but he couldn't do it.

570
00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.910
Now we go upstairs to Nellie's office.

571
00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:03.690
Daryl is going to enter and ask her to sign off on a shipment that's going to go out soon.

572
00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:07.650
Nellie's going to ask Daryl how everything's going in the warehouse, and he says, well, you

573
00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:07.910
know what?

574
00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:10.670
You can go downstairs and check it out for yourself.

575
00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:12.850
And she's like, oh, it's downstairs?

576
00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:14.890
She doesn't know where it is.

577
00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:18.310
Did you notice Nellie's desk chair by any chance?

578
00:24:18.730 --> 00:24:19.290
No.

579
00:24:19.710 --> 00:24:22.630
It's like this taupe-y cream color.

580
00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:23.950
It's like a faux leather.

581
00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:25.030
It's very nice.

582
00:24:25.290 --> 00:24:32.030
It is not the chair that Steve sat in or Ed sat in or Creed, anyone.

583
00:24:32.270 --> 00:24:32.470
Yeah.

584
00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:33.670
It's this new chair.

585
00:24:34.310 --> 00:24:36.630
I became sort of obsessed with it.

586
00:24:36.750 --> 00:24:38.510
I wanted to know, how did this happen?

587
00:24:38.670 --> 00:24:39.810
Where did this chair come from?

588
00:24:39.890 --> 00:24:41.170
When did it come from?

589
00:24:41.670 --> 00:24:44.070
And I fully mom-detectived it.

590
00:24:44.590 --> 00:24:48.230
I don't have a great answer, but I spent a good deal of time on it.

591
00:24:48.330 --> 00:24:49.850
That is mom-detectives.

592
00:24:49.850 --> 00:24:50.390
That is.

593
00:24:50.510 --> 00:24:54.730
We rarely solve our crimes or our mysteries, I should say.

594
00:24:55.130 --> 00:24:57.670
Isn't our slogan, solving crimes no one cares about?

595
00:24:57.850 --> 00:25:01.030
Or sort of solving crimes that no one cares about?

596
00:25:01.330 --> 00:25:03.870
So not necessarily a crime, but a mystery.

597
00:25:04.530 --> 00:25:05.970
Where did this chair come from?

598
00:25:06.130 --> 00:25:09.390
So I went back and I looked to see, when did it appear?

599
00:25:09.390 --> 00:25:12.430
In Get the Girl, it's the old chair.

600
00:25:12.670 --> 00:25:18.250
We don't see her chair in Welcome Party, but then the new chair is there, starting with

601
00:25:18.250 --> 00:25:19.150
Angry Andy.

602
00:25:19.930 --> 00:25:28.290
So I think we can safely say that this new chair came during Welcome Party, when Dwight

603
00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:32.590
and Jim went to her house to unpack her things that had been delivered.

604
00:25:32.590 --> 00:25:38.850
I think that there is something that happened off camera where they brought this new office

605
00:25:38.850 --> 00:25:40.610
chair into the office.

606
00:25:40.830 --> 00:25:44.630
So you think she had the fancy office chair in her apartment?

607
00:25:44.870 --> 00:25:45.230
Yes.

608
00:25:45.470 --> 00:25:50.670
I think it was delivered with her other furniture, and then she moved it in because starting with

609
00:25:50.670 --> 00:25:55.810
Angry Andy, she's really taken over his office, and I think she brought in her new chair.

610
00:25:56.130 --> 00:25:56.430
Okay.

611
00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:58.190
Is it a De Sede?

612
00:25:58.630 --> 00:25:59.150
Chair?

613
00:25:59.390 --> 00:25:59.630
Yeah.

614
00:26:00.590 --> 00:26:01.590
It could be.

615
00:26:01.790 --> 00:26:04.290
It doesn't look ugly enough, in my opinion.

616
00:26:04.290 --> 00:26:08.850
Oh my gosh, you're really laying it out there.

617
00:26:09.070 --> 00:26:12.430
Why am I so mean to this luxury Italian couch?

618
00:26:13.570 --> 00:26:14.750
Something about it.

619
00:26:14.990 --> 00:26:16.770
It just really bumped you.

620
00:26:16.910 --> 00:26:17.630
It bothers me.

621
00:26:17.630 --> 00:26:18.230
I don't know.

622
00:26:18.430 --> 00:26:21.730
It should be the most beautiful couch I've ever seen, in my opinion.

623
00:26:22.050 --> 00:26:23.710
It should be able to drive.

624
00:26:24.250 --> 00:26:25.330
Yes, exactly.

625
00:26:25.630 --> 00:26:26.310
What does the couch do?

626
00:26:26.310 --> 00:26:29.530
She should be able to hit a button and the wheels come out if you take it down the road.

627
00:26:29.950 --> 00:26:32.750
Nellie is now going to have a talking head where she says,

628
00:26:33.130 --> 00:26:36.510
tonight could be the night she and Daryl become good friends.

629
00:26:36.750 --> 00:26:40.830
The only thing in their way is the contempt he feels for her.

630
00:26:41.030 --> 00:26:45.390
So I was wondering, why is it important for Nellie to become friends with Daryl?

631
00:26:45.390 --> 00:26:52.130
And I realized that this is setting up a storyline that's going to pay off in a few episodes,

632
00:26:52.130 --> 00:26:58.830
where you realize that Nellie really doesn't have any friends since she moved to Scranton.

633
00:26:58.930 --> 00:26:59.150
Yeah.

634
00:26:59.410 --> 00:27:01.550
And this is kind of important to her.

635
00:27:01.650 --> 00:27:02.550
I liked this.

636
00:27:02.690 --> 00:27:05.710
I liked that we're planting the seed with this storyline here.

637
00:27:05.990 --> 00:27:07.910
She wants a friend in the office.

638
00:27:08.150 --> 00:27:08.410
Yes.

639
00:27:09.070 --> 00:27:11.150
The fundraiser is now underway.

640
00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:14.630
We're going to see Angela in her outfit.

641
00:27:15.290 --> 00:27:19.010
She's very much wanting to play the part of the senator's wife here.

642
00:27:19.810 --> 00:27:23.670
Robert California walks up and is interrupted by Andy.

643
00:27:24.130 --> 00:27:27.950
And lady, I just wanted you to know this little introduction when Robert walks up.

644
00:27:28.050 --> 00:27:31.370
And Angela greets him and is like, the senator and I just wanted to say hello.

645
00:27:31.690 --> 00:27:32.970
You know, she's doing like that.

646
00:27:32.970 --> 00:27:34.390
That was all improvised.

647
00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:34.890
Oh.

648
00:27:35.290 --> 00:27:38.710
All it said in the script is that everyone says, hi, good to see you.

649
00:27:39.430 --> 00:27:39.930
Oh.

650
00:27:40.550 --> 00:27:41.590
Well, well done.

651
00:27:41.590 --> 00:27:42.450
I liked it.

652
00:27:42.590 --> 00:27:45.630
I was so delighted by this episode.

653
00:27:45.770 --> 00:27:51.230
I just love it when Angela Martin thinks she's fancy and is trying to be fancy.

654
00:27:51.490 --> 00:27:56.550
And every single moment, I just wanted to find some little nugget of something to do

655
00:27:56.550 --> 00:28:01.690
to show how high the stakes were for her to be the senator's wife at this event.

656
00:28:01.690 --> 00:28:05.550
Well, speaking of fancy, fan question from Katie Jo B.

657
00:28:05.910 --> 00:28:07.130
in Indiana.

658
00:28:07.510 --> 00:28:08.590
Hi, Katie Jo.

659
00:28:09.210 --> 00:28:13.550
Angela, how did you feel about your zhuzhed hairdo at the fundraiser?

660
00:28:13.710 --> 00:28:16.750
Did you have an extensive hair meeting like Jenna would have?

661
00:28:17.090 --> 00:28:20.070
Did you love getting to smile so much in this episode?

662
00:28:21.610 --> 00:28:23.730
You know, it was nice to smile.

663
00:28:24.090 --> 00:28:27.750
There is one scene, I will tell you, Katie, where I didn't get to smile.

664
00:28:27.750 --> 00:28:35.010
It got deleted, but we did shoot it where I completely lose it because Andy is ruining

665
00:28:35.010 --> 00:28:35.850
my event.

666
00:28:36.950 --> 00:28:37.470
Yes.

667
00:28:37.470 --> 00:28:39.950
I go to the center and I'm like, he's ruining it.

668
00:28:40.030 --> 00:28:41.030
And I'm just like upset.

669
00:28:41.430 --> 00:28:45.890
But for the most part, I got to smile this whole week, which was lovely.

670
00:28:46.110 --> 00:28:48.670
And we did have a very extensive hair meeting.

671
00:28:48.670 --> 00:28:55.630
I remember the vision they wanted is that Angela Martin wants to be like Jackie Kennedy, right?

672
00:28:56.030 --> 00:29:01.170
She wants that sort of bouffant hair that flipped out at the end, you know?

673
00:29:01.690 --> 00:29:03.890
So yeah, that was our whole look.

674
00:29:04.050 --> 00:29:04.770
I love that.

675
00:29:04.870 --> 00:29:06.610
You guys had a story behind the hairdo.

676
00:29:06.730 --> 00:29:06.950
Yes.

677
00:29:07.050 --> 00:29:11.790
And this is the second time that Angela Martin has tried to look like Jackie Kennedy.

678
00:29:12.130 --> 00:29:12.930
You remember?

679
00:29:12.950 --> 00:29:14.850
She wore the pillbox hat.

680
00:29:15.050 --> 00:29:15.270
Yes.

681
00:29:15.490 --> 00:29:17.090
And the blue suit to Phyllis's wedding.

682
00:29:17.090 --> 00:29:23.350
Something that's interesting to me is, would Angela support the Kennedy politics or it's

683
00:29:23.350 --> 00:29:24.370
just the fashion?

684
00:29:26.050 --> 00:29:28.050
That I'm not sure about.

685
00:29:28.730 --> 00:29:30.870
It's an interesting choice of role model.

686
00:29:31.070 --> 00:29:35.930
I'm surprised that she doesn't fashion herself after Nancy Reagan.

687
00:29:36.170 --> 00:29:38.910
Well, you know, she was Nancy Reagan for Halloween.

688
00:29:39.370 --> 00:29:40.210
This is true.

689
00:29:40.350 --> 00:29:42.950
I think she just wants to be a politician's wife.

690
00:29:43.150 --> 00:29:43.450
Yes.

691
00:29:43.530 --> 00:29:44.330
She doesn't care.

692
00:29:44.330 --> 00:29:45.130
She doesn't care.

693
00:29:45.210 --> 00:29:45.910
The political affiliation.

694
00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:46.490
That's right.

695
00:29:46.490 --> 00:29:50.110
She just, if you have a good suit or a nice hat, she's going to try it out.

696
00:29:50.390 --> 00:29:53.210
I've got a location breakdown for this banquet hall.

697
00:29:53.410 --> 00:29:58.810
We got a fan question from Haley in Austin, Texas asking, where were the fundraiser scenes

698
00:29:58.810 --> 00:29:59.270
shot?

699
00:29:59.830 --> 00:30:03.170
At five minutes and three seconds, there's a shot of the outside of the building.

700
00:30:03.410 --> 00:30:06.450
Is that also the actual building that the scenes were shot in?

701
00:30:06.450 --> 00:30:08.370
These are very savvy questions.

702
00:30:08.710 --> 00:30:10.290
This is a long time listener.

703
00:30:10.630 --> 00:30:13.150
Haley knows that it could be different places.

704
00:30:13.430 --> 00:30:13.790
That's right.

705
00:30:14.330 --> 00:30:16.250
I asked Steve Burgess about this.

706
00:30:16.390 --> 00:30:22.170
He said, we shot the ballroom fundraiser scenes at the Warner Center Marriott in Woodland Hills.

707
00:30:22.750 --> 00:30:24.410
We were there for two days.

708
00:30:25.070 --> 00:30:30.510
Steve said that he remembers sending a camera crew outside one night to get an establishing shot,

709
00:30:30.610 --> 00:30:33.070
but he couldn't find it anywhere on his schedule.

710
00:30:33.070 --> 00:30:37.550
So it is very possible that we used like a stock footage shot of a hotel.

711
00:30:38.150 --> 00:30:44.230
So he's not totally sure, but we did go on location to shoot the fundraiser banquet scenes.

712
00:30:45.070 --> 00:30:49.630
But either way, Steve Burgess said that the banner on the outside of the building,

713
00:30:49.630 --> 00:30:51.070
that was added in poSt.

714
00:30:51.230 --> 00:30:53.790
We did not actually hang a banner on a building.

715
00:30:54.490 --> 00:30:56.130
Andy is now going to have a talking head.

716
00:30:56.350 --> 00:30:57.170
He says, you know what?

717
00:30:57.310 --> 00:30:58.270
Where do I look?

718
00:30:58.470 --> 00:31:01.070
You know, it's been so long since I've done one of these interviews.

719
00:31:01.450 --> 00:31:01.730
Yeah.

720
00:31:01.930 --> 00:31:02.150
Yeah.

721
00:31:02.470 --> 00:31:03.130
How am I doing?

722
00:31:03.290 --> 00:31:04.090
I'm doing great.

723
00:31:04.930 --> 00:31:05.730
Red flag.

724
00:31:05.730 --> 00:31:07.890
I mean, there's so many red flags.

725
00:31:08.690 --> 00:31:08.950
Yeah.

726
00:31:09.170 --> 00:31:10.290
Well, just wait.

727
00:31:10.530 --> 00:31:13.070
There's going to be a flag flurry coming up.

728
00:31:13.270 --> 00:31:14.010
A flag flurry.

729
00:31:14.630 --> 00:31:17.110
Kevin and Creed are going to check out the auction table.

730
00:31:17.550 --> 00:31:21.890
And that's when Dwight is going to come up and tell them that they're doing it all wrong,

731
00:31:21.990 --> 00:31:22.730
that they're idiots.

732
00:31:23.090 --> 00:31:23.230
Yeah.

733
00:31:23.490 --> 00:31:25.890
They haven't guessed the correct price of anything.

734
00:31:26.490 --> 00:31:30.250
And Kevin tries to correct Dwight, but Dwight is just taking over.

735
00:31:30.450 --> 00:31:32.870
He's just writing down a bunch of amounts.

736
00:31:32.870 --> 00:31:34.490
And Kevin's like, okay, fine.

737
00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:39.070
Kevin has a talking head where he says, Dwight doesn't understand what a silent auction is,

738
00:31:39.190 --> 00:31:41.810
which means he's the stupid guy in the office.

739
00:31:42.050 --> 00:31:43.870
Up till now, they didn't have one.

740
00:31:44.290 --> 00:31:47.550
Can I tell you, that was not the scripted talking head.

741
00:31:47.710 --> 00:31:48.570
It wasn't?

742
00:31:48.710 --> 00:31:49.210
It wasn't.

743
00:31:49.350 --> 00:31:51.330
That was the candy bag alt.

744
00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:54.290
The scripted talking head was this.

745
00:31:54.810 --> 00:31:55.150
Huh.

746
00:31:55.330 --> 00:31:56.610
I know more than Dwight.

747
00:31:56.910 --> 00:31:58.110
You know what they say.

748
00:31:58.310 --> 00:32:00.510
Even a clock is right once a day.

749
00:32:01.070 --> 00:32:01.590
Oh.

750
00:32:01.590 --> 00:32:03.930
And they went with the candy bag alt.

751
00:32:04.070 --> 00:32:07.030
Which is very funny because the saying is that a clock is right twice a day.

752
00:32:07.210 --> 00:32:10.610
A broken clock is right twice a day.

753
00:32:10.810 --> 00:32:10.970
Right?

754
00:32:11.250 --> 00:32:12.110
Isn't that the saying?

755
00:32:12.190 --> 00:32:12.810
I don't know.

756
00:32:12.930 --> 00:32:17.130
But yeah, I thought this was a great example of when they actually went with one of the

757
00:32:17.130 --> 00:32:20.050
alts and didn't use the one that was in the shooting draft.

758
00:32:20.410 --> 00:32:25.650
Well, I really like the detail of seeing Dwight guessing prices in the background of Kevin's

759
00:32:25.650 --> 00:32:29.370
talking head, and I went to the script, and I noticed that that was not scripted.

760
00:32:29.470 --> 00:32:33.250
That was a directing choice by Dave Rogers, and I absolutely loved it.

761
00:32:33.310 --> 00:32:35.510
It really added to the realism of the moment for me.

762
00:32:35.950 --> 00:32:40.410
You know, my husband is very, very good at guessing prices of things.

763
00:32:40.790 --> 00:32:42.810
Like he would kill it on The Prices Right?

764
00:32:42.810 --> 00:32:43.790
He would kill it.

765
00:32:43.910 --> 00:32:45.250
I went on The Prices Right.

766
00:32:45.250 --> 00:32:48.210
I didn't make it up on the stage, but when I first moved to L.A.

767
00:32:48.330 --> 00:32:49.230
You were in the audience?

